# Technical Content Contribution Guide

This section provides information on editing documentation on a repository.

## Step-by-Step Contribution Workflow

### 1. Fork & Branch the Repository
Clone the repository locally and create a feature branch:
```bash
git checkout -b docs/fix-my-token-expiration
```

### 2. Adhere to Content Guidelines
*   Keep files structured using standard Markdown headings.
*   Use standard code-block syntaxes accompanied by the correct programming language flag (e.g., ` ```javascript `).
*   Run local lint tests to ensure the content matches the project styles:
    ```bash
    npm run docs:lint
    ```

### 3. Open a Pull Request (PR)
Push the local branch to the remote infrastructure tracking workspace and open a clear Pull Request:
*   Clearly state the problem the documentation fix resolves.
*   Link any relevant tracking tickets (e.g., Closes issue `#4321`).
*   Assign at least one Senior Technical Writer and one Engineering Subject Matter Expert (SME) to review the content.

### 4. Merge Changes
Merge the updates with the main branch:
```bash
git merge docs/fix-my-token-expiration
```

### 5. Safely Delete the Branch
Delete the temporary branch created for updates:
```bash
git branch -d docs/fix-my-token-expiration
```
